// weyland-platform-worker/src/lib/marketing-pages.js
//
// Deliberate SUBSET fork of ../../../src/lib/marketing-pages.js's
// SovereignWeylandRoutes IIFE. The source file's dispatch map has ~40
// entries - one per not-yet-built "X-tool" teaser page (WeatherX, GeoX,
// CompX, LienX, BidX, CoA, RFAx, ...) plus the 6 already-extracted
// products' own marketing pages (huntx, subx, propx, cutsheetx, sightx,
// meetingx - now served by their own standalone Workers via Cloudflare
// Routes, making the monolith's copies unreachable for those paths
// already). This platform Worker's task scope is the root marketing
// page, /pricing, and /subscribe - NOT the other ~35 teaser pages, which
// are a separate, not-yet-scoped extraction. Only ROUTE_LABELS, renderNav,
// serve_whyweyland ("" - the real root marketing page), serve_pricing,
// and serve_subscribe are ported below, copied byte-for-byte from the
// source (including their embedded HTML/CSS/JS) - not retyped, to avoid
// exactly the transcription-error risk the source file's own header
// comments warn about for this kind of data. ROUTE_LABELS/renderNav are
// copied in full (not trimmed to just this Worker's 3 pages) because
// serve_whyweyland calls renderNav("whyweyland"), which iterates the
// whole label table to build the nav bar - trimming it would silently
// remove nav links to every other live page on the site.
//
// dispatch() below is narrowed to only the 3 keys this Worker owns
// ("", "pricing", "subscribe") rather than porting all ~40 map entries -
// this Worker's Cloudflare Routes (see wrangler.toml) only ever forward
// these 3 path shapes here, so a wider map would be dead code that could
// silently drift from the source's real ~35-entry map over time.

